<title>USA: PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 nuke nears full power.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L Susquehanna 2 nuke nears full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power and Light Co's 1,094 megawatt (MW) Susquehanna 2 nuclear power unit is ramping up after being reduced to about 80 percent power late Thursday, the company said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll be at 100 percent later today. We're at about 925 megawatts right now,&quot; company spokesman Herb Woodeschick said.</p>
<p>The unit, in Berwick, Pa., was reduced to repair one of the hydrogen recombiners, which mix the hydrogen and oxygen to produce water, he said.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 1,090 MW, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>(( New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
